      "description": "The secondary API path inherits its surrounding field ink and underlines on hover.",
      "html": "<a class=\"ds-text-action\" href=\"/docs/api-reference\">Explore the API <svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6\"/></svg></a>",
      "css": ".ds-text-action{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:14px;min-height:44px;padding:10px 18px;border-radius:var(--radius,.375rem);font:600 .875rem/1.7 \"Inter Variable\",sans-serif;text-decoration:none;padding:0;color:var(--hero-foreground,#103a71)}.ds-text-action:hover{text-decoration:underline}.ds-text-action:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--ring,#1550b9);outline-offset:4px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Search field",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "search-field",
      "description": "The header’s muted search surface; full-width input with a reserved keyboard-hint area.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-search\"><input class=\"ds-search-input\" type=\"search\" aria-label=\"Search documentation\" placeholder=\"Search documentation\"><kbd class=\"ds-search-key\">⌘ K</kbd></div>",
      "css": ".ds-search{position:relative;width:min(360px,100%);color:var(--foreground,#112a45)}.ds-search-input{width:100%;height:38px;padding:4px 32px 4px 10px;border:1px solid var(--border,#c9d9eb);border-radius:var(--radius,.375rem);background:var(--muted,#eaf1fa);color:inherit;font:400 .875rem \"Inter Variable\",sans-serif;transition:color .15s,box-shadow .15s}.ds-search-input::placeholder{color:var(--muted-foreground,#48617d)}.ds-search-input:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--ring,#1550b9);outline-offset:4px;border-color:var(--ring,#1550b9);box-shadow:0 0 0 3px color-mix(in srgb,var(--ring,#1550b9) 50%,transparent)}.ds-search-key{position:absolute;right:12px;top:9px;font-size:.7rem;color:var(--muted-foreground,#48617d);pointer-events:none}@media(max-width:767px){.ds-search-input{height:40px;font-size:1rem}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-search-input{transition-duration:.01ms}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sidebar navigation",
      "kind": "nav",
      "description": "Active items use primary ink, accent fill, and a stronger weight; corners follow the selected identity.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-nav\" aria-label=\"Documentation\"><a class=\"ds-nav-item\" href=\"/docs/getting-started\" aria-current=\"page\">Getting started</a><a class=\"ds-nav-item\" href=\"/docs/events-and-slices\">Events and slices</a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-nav{display:grid;gap:4px;font:400 .8125rem \"Inter Variable\",sans-serif}.ds-nav-item{display:flex;align-items:center;min-height:34px;padding:8px;border-radius:var(--radius,.375rem);color:var(--sidebar-foreground,#112a45);text-decoration:none}.ds-nav-item:hover{background:var(--sidebar-accent,#daeafa);color:var(--sidebar-accent-foreground,#163b68)}.ds-nav-item[aria-current=page]{background:var(--accent,#daeafa);color:var(--primary,#1550b9);font-weight:650}.ds-nav-item:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--ring,#1550b9);outline-offset:4px;}@media(max-width:767px){.ds-nav-item{min-height:40px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Documentation note",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "note",
      "description": "A flat, muted callout with an accent label and compact explanatory prose.",
      "html": "<aside class=\"ds-note\"><strong class=\"ds-note-label\">Store ownership</strong><p class=\"ds-note-copy\">The store creator owns disposal.</p></aside>",
      "css": ".ds-note{padding:20px 22px;border-radius:var(--radius,.375rem);background:var(--muted,#eaf1fa);color:var(--foreground,#112a45);font-family:\"Inter Variable\",sans-serif}.ds-note-label{font-size:.75rem;color:var(--primary,#1550b9)}.ds-note-copy{margin:5px 0 0;font-size:.8125rem;line-height:1.8}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Source region",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "source-panel",
      "description": "A shared dark source sample; Ledger’s introduction changes this region to its muted paper surface. Selectable code keeps horizontal keyboard scrolling.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-source\"><div class=\"ds-source-heading\"><h3 class=\"ds-source-title\">Source</h3><span>counter.ts</span></div><pre class=\"ds-source-code\" tabindex=\"0\"><code>builder.addHandler(increment, (state, { payload }) =&gt; {\n  state.value += payload;\n});</code></pre></section>",
      "css": ".ds-source{padding:16px 20px;background:var(--code,#0d2442);color:var(--code-foreground,#eef5ff)}.ds-source-heading{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-bottom:15px;font:400 .6875rem \"Inter Variable\",sans-serif;color:#b8cdeb}.ds-source-title{margin:0;font-size:.75rem;font-weight:550}.ds-source-code{margin:0;max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto;font:.75rem/1.9 var(--font-mono,\"Geist Mono Variable\",monospace);tab-size:2;scrollbar-color:#54739a var(--code,#0d2442)}.ds-source-code:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--ring,#1550b9);outline-offset:4px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Live state readout",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "A static styling sample of the real counter’s paired state and derived value; the application supplies the store and event behavior.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-readout\"><div class=\"ds-reading\"><span class=\"ds-reading-label\">state.counter.value</span><output class=\"ds-reading-value\" aria-label=\"Counter value\">1</output></div><div class=\"ds-reading\"><span class=\"ds-reading-label\">createMemo(() =&gt; value * 2)</span><output class=\"ds-reading-value\" aria-label=\"Doubled value\">2</output></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-readout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px;padding:18px;background:var(--surface,#fff);color:var(--foreground,#112a45)}.ds-reading+.ds-reading{padding-left:25px;border-left:1px solid var(--border,#c9d9eb)}.ds-reading-label{display:block;font:.6875rem/1.6 var(--font-mono,\"Geist Mono Variable\",monospace);color:var(--muted-foreground,#48617d);overflow-wrap:anywhere}.ds-reading-value{display:block;margin-top:5px;font:600 3rem/1.2 var(--font-heading,\"Onest\",sans-serif);letter-spacing:-.035em;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}@media(max-width:767px){.ds-reading+.ds-reading{padding-left:16px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Event-flow step",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "An emphasized event step illustrates the implemented data-active state. The application derives emphasis from the latest real event.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-flow\"><div class=\"ds-flow-step\" data-active=\"true\"><span class=\"ds-flow-label\">Event</span><code class=\"ds-flow-code\">counter/increment</code></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-flow{border-block:1px solid var(--hero-border,#a6c9ee);color:var(--hero-foreground,#103a71);background:var(--hero-background,#dceefe)}.ds-flow-step{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;min-width:0;padding:14px 12px;font:.8125rem/1.6 \"Inter Variable\",sans-serif}.ds-flow-step[data-active=true]{color:var(--primary,#1550b9);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--hero-foreground,#103a71) 7%,transparent)}.ds-flow-label,.ds-flow-code{color:var(--hero-muted,#31577f);font-size:.6875rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.ds-flow-code{font-family:var(--font-mono,\"Geist Mono Variable\",monospace)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Three provisional Solux identities",
    "overview": "This records three built proposals for comparison: **Blue Workshop**, **Event Ledger**, and **Signal Atlas**, selected by `?design=workshop`, `?design=ledger`, and `?design=atlas`. Their names describe the current implementation; none is a user-approved final identity. Blue Workshop is the fallback when the URL has no valid design value. The user will choose a proposal and iterate after comparing the builds.\n\nThe shared visual foundation supports precise developer documentation: readable prose, inspectable source, visible state, and direct controls. Blue Workshop combines an open sky-blue field with cobalt and Onest. Event Ledger combines warm paper, blue annotation, Manrope, compact corners, and ruled boundaries. Signal Atlas combines a navy field, ivory type, Manrope, connected event steps, and more rounded instruments.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Three provisional identities share one working application and semantic token layer.",
      "Display type supplies identity; Inter carries reading and interface text; Geist Mono carries source.",
      "Color fields, rules, and paired source/state regions provide structure with little elevation.",
      "The existing Solux SVG remains the logo and favicon; this comparison introduces no generated rasters."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Independent Controls Rule",
        "body": "`html[data-design=\"workshop\"|\"ledger\"|\"atlas\"]` selects identity; `.dark` independently selects color mode. Preserve both controls and resolve colors through the semantic custom properties.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Reading Face Rule",
        "body": "Keep display identity in headings and the brand; use Inter for prose and Geist Mono for source. Real state outputs use tabular numerals.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Structural Depth Rule",
        "body": "Use the existing surface, border, and field roles to distinguish regions; reserve floating elevation for the implemented popover and overlay roles.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** retain the three proposal names and provisional status until the user chooses an identity.",
      "**Do** use the active identity's semantic colors and radius across reading pages and controls.",
      "**Do** preserve visible keyboard focus, reduced-motion behavior, and English/French control parity.",
      "**Do** keep source inspectable and state feedback tied to the working example."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** treat Blue Workshop's fallback URL behavior as user approval.",
      "**Don't** combine identity selection with the independent light/dark control.",
      "**Don't** replace the existing Solux logo or SVG favicon.",
      "**Don't** promote a first-surface composition or this provisional comparison bar into an approved global identity."
    ]
  }
}
